First things first.  You didn't see any scrolls of enchant weapon or 
remove curse on the ground of the sanctum.  Fine.  But did you visit 
every square before the crowd?  Magic traps have a possibility for an 
uncurse effect.  That would be the most positive solution.

After that, the possibilities are either: a monster with a bullwhip 
swiping it (I think.)  A monster with a theft attack (nymphs only).  A 
giant, generated on the vibrating square level, hurling a boulder at you 
across the moat.  Pushing the boulder, it fills in the moat, then you 
*plunk* in and wait for luck to end you up on the other side.  Or a 
monster with a frost attack or wand of cold is generated, bridging the 
moat for you.  Or cancelling yourself.  (I'm assuming you don't have a 
wand of cold out, yourself).

That last resort is not as bad as it sounds.  You drop everything you 
don't want to cancel, and afterwards you've got an uncursed wielded 
unicorn horn, and you lost 30 AC, which is at least 10 blessed scrolls 
of enchant armor.  You're at -16 AC, which is light, but only a couple 
scrolls away from the -20's where things are OK if you proceed with care.

So, no, you aren't screwed, and you learned a very expensive lesson. 
Unihorns are two handed, two handed cursed weapons *REALLY* suck, and 
jumping boots are cool.  (Ok, I'm adding that last one.  Jumping boots 
and a light source would hop you across the moat.)

Good luck!

